{"availability":"available","full":"dappforce/subsocial-js","name":"subsocial-js","description":"JavaScript SDK for Subsocial blockchain.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":28,"forks":16,"created":"2020-02-25T20:03:33Z","updated":"2024-08-31T01:44:42Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://docs.subsocial.network/docs/develop","topics":["dappforce","decentralized-communities","javascript-libs","kusama","kusama-network","npm","polkadot","polkadot-js","polkadot-network","subsocial","substrate"],"demo":"https://play.subsocial.network/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:36.897Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:36.897Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:36.897Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T20:15:36.897Z","stars":28,"forks":16}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Subsocial's JS SDK is a library for building social networking applications on top of the Subsocial blockchain. The library will help developers easily interact with the Subsocial blockchain from their UI, without prior knowledge of Subsocial’s pallet implementations. Inside the library, you will find the APIs required to perform different operations on the blockchain, which are detailed here.","Subsocial provides the back-end tech, allowing for easy deployment of decentralized social dapps that share a social graph and content base. Users own their content and social connections on Subsocial, which automatically solves most of the problems of web2 social networks. Applications built on Subsocial do not have to be specifically focused on social networking, as Subsocial can support dapps like YouTube, Shopify, or even Airbnb. You can learn more about Subsocial by reading the lightpaper."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dappforce/subsocial-js/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"bdf53add433117f0c45997aa385578dc31a873482d0bfbba58cc8a62f3f70f19","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:36.988Z"},"ov